From: blender-web contributors
Subject: USD: allow core-only web IO and redraw the first published screen

OpenUSD's scene-description core supports real UsdGeomMesh import/export
without Imaging or Boost.Python. Make those two capabilities explicit while
preserving the native defaults, provide a no-Python hook implementation, and
fall procedural shape prims back to transforms when Imaging is unavailable.

On Emscripten, a surface can publish its clear before Blender's regions have
received their first redraw tag. The web GHOST backend sends bounded ordinary
WindowUpdate events until the second present; invalidate the screen for those
events so the second publish contains the UI. Native event behavior is
unchanged.

